GPU: let kept buffers go when the address space is full; log the space and who holds what (0177).

RedwoodGPU keeps up to 160 MB of freed GPU buffers per program (gpu_keep, 60 s), wired and
mapped in the one 512 MiB GPU address space all programs share, and let them go only when the
same program made a new buffer. Logs: "MB kept" up to 137 MB for one program (live-sileo1),
"no addresses left for a buffer of 8912896 bytes" (51 in live-sileo1, 123 in live-gpucache1),
then "texture refused: texture: OutOfMemory(Device)" in com.apple.WebKit.GPU.

- gpu_reclaim=1 (default): a buffer that finds no run (or no slot) lets kept buffers of all
  programs go (those at least as big first, oldest first) and tries again; kept buffers older
  than 60 s are let go in every program each 5 s stats period. gpu_reclaim=0: as before.
- gpu_keep_mb=N (default 0 = off): at most N MB kept by all programs together.
- spesgpu_va_mb=N (default 512, at most 960): the space continues into L2 entries 0-223 of
  the second GiB (0x40000000-0x5bffffff, below the FB table at 0x5c000000).
- spesgpu_va_fit=1 (default 0): best fit instead of first fit.
- Log: "RedwoodGPU: space: ..." every stats period (the old gpu_va line never printed: nothing
  sets gpu_va on spes), "RedwoodGPU: client PID NAME: own/surfaces/host/kept/left ..." every
  30 s and after a refusal, "RedwoodGPU: reclaim for N bytes ..." on each reclaim (rate-limited).
  The backend ready line names the VA range and the fit.

